@@ -0,0 +1,92 @@
+# Native CMake build and validation
+
+R1 uses one canonical CMake library target for native development and validation:
+
+```cmake
+openVFIFE::openvfife
+```
+
+The concrete target is a static library named `openvfife`. Shared-library export
+and installed-package mechanics are intentionally deferred to the packaging work
+in #47.
+
+## Requirements
+
+- CMake 3.20 or newer.
+- A compiler with C++20 language support. The R1 implementation is validated with
+  GCC 14.2.0; GCC and Clang receive the project warning/hardening/sanitizer flags.
+- Python 3.8 or newer when `BUILD_TESTING=ON`, for the frozen Fortran comparisons.
+- No network access is required by configure or build. R1 uses the bundled Eigen
+  3.4.0 tree through the `openVFIFE::eigen` interface target.
+
+Project warning, hardening, `-Werror`, and sanitizer options are PRIVATE to
+openVFIFE-owned targets. They are not usage requirements imposed on downstream
+consumers.
+
+## Native validation
+
+The reproducible entry point is:
+
+```bash
+bash scripts/build_native_tests.sh
+```
+
+Equivalent explicit commands are:
+
+```bash
+cmake -S . -B build/native \
+  -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release \
+  -DBUILD_TESTING=ON \
+  -DOPENVFIFE_ENABLE_SANITIZERS=OFF \
+  -DOPENVFIFE_ENABLE_HARDENING=ON
+cmake --build build/native --parallel
+ctest --test-dir build/native --output-on-failure -L native
+```
+
+Set `CXX` to select a compiler before the first configure. The wrapper also accepts
+`OPENVFIFE_BUILD_DIR` and `OPENVFIFE_BUILD_TYPE`.
+
+CTest runs the existing Beam2D/Beam3D, unit, shim, and both frozen parity checks.
+The parity probes write CSV under the configured build directory and compare it
+against the checked-in Fortran evidence; the comparison does not regenerate or
+change fixtures or tolerances.
+
+## ASan + UBSan validation
+
+The sanitizer configuration has its own build directory so the core library is
+compiled with instrumentation rather than reusing native objects:
+
+```bash
+bash scripts/build_native_sanitizers.sh
+```
+
+Equivalent explicit commands are:
+
+```bash
+cmake -S . -B build/sanitizers \
+  -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=RelWithDebInfo \
+  -DBUILD_TESTING=ON \
+  -DOPENVFIFE_ENABLE_SANITIZERS=ON \
+  -DOPENVFIFE_ENABLE_HARDENING=OFF
+cmake --build build/sanitizers --parallel --target openvfife_sanitizer_targets
+ASAN_OPTIONS=detect_leaks=1:halt_on_error=1 \
+UBSAN_OPTIONS=halt_on_error=1:print_stacktrace=1 \
+ctest --test-dir build/sanitizers --output-on-failure -L sanitizer
+```
+
+`-fsanitize=address,undefined` is applied while compiling the `openvfife` core and
+validation objects, and again on validation executable link steps. The sanitizer
+label preserves the pre-CMake fast sanitizer surface: Beam2D, focused unit tests,
+and both frozen parity probes. Beam3D and the native shim remain part of normal
+native validation, matching the previous scripts.
+
+The wrapper accepts `OPENVFIFE_SANITIZER_BUILD_DIR` and
+`OPENVFIFE_SANITIZER_BUILD_TYPE`; `ASAN_OPTIONS` and `UBSAN_OPTIONS` remain
+overridable by the caller.
+
+## Build ownership
+
+The seven production `.cpp` files are listed once, on the `openvfife` target.
+Every native validation executable links `openVFIFE::openvfife`. The native shim is
+an object target that consumes the same library and no longer owns a duplicate core
+source list. The legacy Emscripten entry point is deliberately left for #48.
